LOCAL VALIDATION (API-LEVEL ONLY — NOT browser evidence)
Executed on this VM before the first CI run, to validate the
driver's assertion EXPECTATIONS against the real server (the VM
cannot launch Chromium; the runner is the browser environment).

1. Driver compiles: python3 -m py_compile gui/browser_acceptance.py OK
   Workflow YAML parses OK (yaml.safe_load).
2. Server launched locally: python3 -m gui.server --owner
   BrowserLocal --port 8765 (loopback default), killed by PID after.
   - Served / carries a substituted per-launch token in the
     studio-token meta (NOT the __STUDIO_TOKEN__ placeholder).
   - GET /api/dells -> ok=True, count=100.
   - POST /api/parse (token header, as app.js sends) for the
     driver's example seed "55[Set] :: tempo=120 >> 56[Get] :: tempo"
     -> parse ok=True, atoms=[55, 56].
   - POST /api/execute (same seed) -> ok=True,
     atom_results=[(55, True), (56, True)], store={'tempo': '120'}.
   These are the exact values the browser assertions then verified
   through the DOM on the runner (rack 100; 2 atoms; 2 atom-ok;
   CHAIN OK; store shows tempo/120).
3. Driver failure path, local: with no CDP listener it prints
   "[FAIL] CDP target list reachable" and exits 1 (bounded wait),
   i.e. the driver fails closed rather than passing vacuously.
